Hm, interesting that this is allowed in pydantic even if `Mixin` is not a model itself. We currently don't have special support for pydantic. I'll add this as a child issue of #2403.

In the meantime, you could use the following to make this work with both pydantic (hopefully) and ty. Note the reversed base class order on `MyModel`

```py
from pydantic import BaseModel, Field


class Mixin(BaseModel):
    mixin_field: bool = Field(default=...)


class MyModel(Mixin, BaseModel):
    model_field: bool = Field(default=...)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    print(MyModel(model_field=True, mixin_field=False).model_dump())```

