query:
class `Just` does not work for `ty` when it comes to `Just[float]`

### Summary

We have a class `Just` from https://discuss.python.org/t/type-hints-for-bool-vs-int-overload/72239/21 which excludes `bool` from `int`, `bool` and `int` from `float`, etc. `Just[float]` works with `mypy`, `pyright` and `pyrefly`, but not with `ty`.

https://play.ty.dev/1bf6e98f-fa91-4723-ae4f-ef0cb7de6036

```py
from datetime import datetime
from typing import override, Protocol, Generic, TypeVar, Self, assert_type

T = TypeVar("T")


class Just(Protocol, Generic[T]):
    @property
    @override
    def __class__(self, /) -> type[T]: ...
    @__class__.setter
    @override
    def __class__(self, t: type[T], /) -> None: ...


class Timestamp:
    def __mul__(self, other: Just[float]) -> Self:
        return self


assert_type(Timestamp() * 1.1, Timestamp)  # ty gives Unknown

```

