query:
Narrowing gradual types with static protocols

As described [here](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/28193#discussion_r3935574152), we currently emit an error on this snippet:

```py
from typing import Any, Literal, Protocol, TypeIs, overload

class Source:
    @overload
    def read(self, key: Literal["value"]) -> object: ...
    @overload
    def read(self, key: str) -> Any: ...
    def read(self, key: str) -> Any:
        raise NotImplementedError

class IntReader(Protocol):
    def read(self, key: str) -> int: ...

def is_int_reader(x: object) -> TypeIs[IntReader]:
    raise NotImplementedError

def f(x: Source):
    if is_int_reader(x):
        value: int = x.read("value")  # invalid-assignment
```

All other type checkers error on this snippet as well, but it seems reasonable to intersect `Source & IntReader` here, which would then lead to `object & int = int` for the `x.read("value")` call.

The same issue exists for `isinstance` narrowing (`isinstance(x, Reader)` with a `@runtime_checkable` `IntReader`).

(related: https://github.com/astral-sh/ty/issues/4480)

