query:
Implicit dunder calls do not retain intersection receivers

Compared to *explicit* dunder calls, implicit dunder calls do not retain intersection type receivers, so we reveal `MyCallable` here instead of `MyCallable & Other`

```py
from typing import Self

class MyCallable:
    def __call__(self) -> Self:
        raise

class Other: ...

def example(c: MyCallable):
    if isinstance(c, Other):
        reveal_type(c.__call__())  # MyCallable & Other
        reveal_type(c())           # MyCallable
```

